    "description": "AttachmentService is one of several services in a document-processing platform. Every request may include a tenant document identifier, but only about five percent request an archived attachment. AttachmentService currently creates a GatewaySession during construction, validates remote credentials, and reserves a channel from the archive gateway. Session establishment takes roughly 1.5 seconds, the shared gateway permits only twelve channels, and each service instance currently consumes one even when no attachment is ever requested. Credential problems in the archive subsystem also prevent otherwise healthy instances from passing startup checks. The public call to retrieveAttachment must remain unchanged for callers. The service should establish at most one session when the first archive request arrives, reuse it for later requests, synchronize concurrent first calls, and release it during controlled shutdown. Creating the session after a request arrives is acceptable even though the first such request becomes slower. The metadata service must remain operational when the archive gateway is unavailable, and a one-shot command that definitely reads one attachment should not retain a channel longer than necessary.",
    "decision_statement": "Decide whether the archive gateway session should be acquired during service construction or only when an attachment is first requested, while preventing duplicate concurrent acquisitions and preserving shutdown behavior.",
    "notes": "Replaced construct-on-first-use, whose static-init-order problem is absent here, with lazy-initialization and eager-acquisition: deferral-of-a-value is the true near miss and eager construction is the decision's explicit rejected alternative."
  },
